# Copy to `.dev.vars` (git-ignored) to run the Worker locally.
#
# The origin the browser uses. It must match the port Vite actually serves on,
# or sign-in redirects land somewhere the session cookie does not exist.
APP_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5175

# Show sign-in links and codes in the app instead of mailing them.
# Only works together with the two conditions below, so it cannot leak in production.
DEV_ECHO_LINKS=1

# Your own address, if you want to reach the administration page locally.
# In production this is a secret, not a var — a personal address does not
# belong in `wrangler.toml`, which anyone who can read the repository can read.
# ADMIN_EMAIL=you@example.org

# RESEND_API_KEY is deliberately absent.
#
# Echo mode above requires that there is no key, that this flag is `1`, and
# that the request host is localhost. Putting even a placeholder key here
# switches echo mode off and breaks sign-in locally — it has happened.
#
# The real key and CODE_PEPPER are production secrets, set by hand with
# `wrangler secret put`, and never live in a file.
